<title>VENEZUELA: Santander closes Venezuela bank deal for $351 mln.</title>
<headline>Santander closes Venezuela bank deal for $351 mln.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish bank Banco Santander said Friday it had a formalized its December bid for leading Venezuelan bank Banco Venezuela paying $351 million for a 93.38 percent share.</p>
<p>Santander successfully bid for the bank December 19, putting up $338.4 million for a 90 percent share.</p>
<p>Under original Venezuelan government plans, twenty percent of the bank was to be sold to small local investors.</p>
<p>Less than seven percent was finally bought, but under the terms of the sale Santander was to pay for the remainder.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
